{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sopāka (1st)","html":"<article id='thag1.33'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.33 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.33 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sopākattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sopāka (1st) </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yathāpi ekaputtasmiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Just as a mother would be good </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>piyasmiṁ kusalī siyā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>to her beloved only child; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ sabbesu pāṇesu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so, to creatures all and everywhere, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sabbattha kusalo siyā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>let one be good. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sopāko thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
